<title>USA: Wash. Gov. unveils plan to cut costs, build schools.</title>
<headline>Wash. Gov. unveils plan to cut costs, build schools.</headline>
<dateline>OLYMPIA, Wash. 1997-02-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>Washington Gov. Gary Locke outlined a program on Wednesday that would encourage state agencies to cut costs and provide additional funds to build schools.</p>
<p>Locke's office said the program would reward state agencies for cost-cutting by returning to them a portion of the state savings.</p>
<p>Additional funds from the so-called &quot;Savings Incentive Plan&quot; would be used for school construction projects in the state, Locke said.</p>
<p>Locke's program is expected to save the general fund $85.5 million in the 1997-1999 biennium. The savings would grow to $99.2 million in the 2001-2003 budget period, his office said in a statement.</p>
